    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2010 Incoterms 2020, the seller (in Seoul) is responsible for delivering the goods to a carrier, exporting them from South Korea, and paying all costs and risks associated with transporting them to Hamburg. However, the seller must still arrange and pay for the main carriage and insurance to Hamburg, despite the risk of loss or damage passing to the buyer once the goods are loaded on the vessel at the port of shipment. Crucially, while the seller handles the logistics and expenses to Hamburg, they have no obligation to deliver the goods there safely if something goes wrong during transit; that risk transfers to the buyer immediately upon delivery at the port of shipment (Seoulvin).",
